// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27os/opencode_free.t27 -- the OpenCode free pool as a second executor: which models a lane may
; use, which content a model may receive, which jobs go to the pool, and what a lane does when the pool
; says "no more". Pure decisions only; the host that calls the catalog and the models is T27 OS, and
; the cell, the key chain and the failover it extends are specs/t27os/agents.t27 (AG_OPENCODE, cell 3)
; and specs/t27os/keys.t27 (RATE_COOLDOWN_S, imported below, not copied).
; Owner request 2026-10-31 (translated): connect OpenCode as a second executor and use its free
; models to raise the volume of work at the same paid budget; the free models are read from the live
; catalog, never hardcoded; a model that needs a paid key or spends paid credits is not free. Owner
; "go" 2026-10-31 (translated) with four conditions: no paid model in a lane; non-public content only
; to glm-5.3-flash-free and deepseek-v4.1-flash-free; nothing is updated or installed; exactly one
; probe per model, with no repository content. Issue: t27#12975 (Refs #12974, #12973, #12945, #7718).
; --
; THE CATALOG (the host reads it; this spec only judges what it read). GET /zen/v1/models on
; opencode.ai answers 200 with no key; each record under .data carries the price of a million tokens
; in .cost.text.input.price and .cost.text.output.price. A model is FREE when both prices are zero:
; the suffix "-free" is not the test (big-pickle is free without it, and a "-free" name with a price is
; not free), and the models.dev mirror is not the source (it is stale). The host converts each price
; to nano-dollars per million tokens ROUNDED UP, so any nonzero price stays nonzero, and passes
; PRICE_UNKNOWN for a missing field: an absent price is never zero. The list is read at run time and
; stamped; no model id is a constant of this spec except the two the owner named and the data table
; below, which only ever restricts.
; --
; RECEIPTS, 2026-10-31 (public-safe, no key and no repository content in any of it):
; - Catalog: 8 of 78 models were free: big-pickle, beam-free, flint-40b-free, mimo-v2.6-flash-free,
;   nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free, nemotron-3.5-lightning-free, deepseek-v4.1-flash-free,
;   glm-5.3-flash-free. All speak chat-completions.
; - Data use (docs.opencode.ai/zen, read the same day): glm-5.3-flash-free and deepseek-v4.1-flash-free
;   keep no data and do not train; beam-free does not train but keeps data for 30 days and is closed
;   to some regions; big-pickle, flint-40b-free and mimo-v2.6-flash-free may use data to improve the
;   model; the two Nemotron free models are not established.
; - Probe: one request per free model, the prompt "Reply with the single word ok.", the keyless public
;   token, no repository content. All eight answered HTTP 429 with the error type FreeUsageLimitError
;   ("Free usage limit reached") and the same Retry-After, about 62 220 s, i.e. one shared reset near
;   2026-11-01T00:00:20Z. No x-ratelimit headers. So the limit is a property of the pool, not of a
;   model: rotating from one free model to another buys nothing. The allowance was already used up
;   when first probed; its size per day is not published and not measured. Measured free capacity at
;   2026-10-31T06:43Z: zero until that reset.
; --
; THE RULES.
; 1. A lane may use a model only if lane_ok(): provider opencode (Zen) or nvidia, both prices zero, and
;    the content allowed for that model. No paid model is selectable, whatever the environment holds.
; 2. Content has four classes. Nothing (a probe) and public text may go to any free model. Non-public
;    text goes only to the two models the owner named. A secret goes to none: it never leaves the
;    machine, and an unknown class is treated as a secret.
; 3. A job goes to the pool, to Claude, or to the owner by its class (route_task). Security-critical
;    work stays on Claude unless the owner approved it for the pool; secrets, credentials, deletion,
;    upstream, publication and payment are the owner's and no lane starts them.
; 4. A free-usage-limit answer puts the whole pool to wait for the time the server gave; any other
;    429 puts that model to wait at least RATE_COOLDOWN_S. Nobody calls a waiting lane, nobody loops
;    on a retry, and a probe is allowed only once per model and never while the pool waits.
; 5. A model that leaves the catalog, or stops being free, is UNAVAILABLE and stays so until a fresh
;    catalog lists it free again. A substitute is a new lane_ok() decision, never a silent swap.
; 6. The card shows a free model as free, or as limited by quota; never as unlimited capacity.
; 7. NVIDIA (owner, 2026-10-31, translated: "we have free NVIDIA tokens, connect their models in
;    OpenCode"). The same law, with three differences. (a) A NVIDIA model starts UNPROVEN: a listed
;    price of 0 is not an entitlement, so it gets one content-free probe and no work until that probe
;    answers 200 with text. (b) HTTP 401, 402 or 403 puts that model in NO_ENTITLEMENT, which a fresh
;    listing does not lift; only the owner's re-arm does. (c) NVIDIA models get a probe or public text
;    and nothing else, whatever their name: the owner's two non-public models are Zen models, and
;    NVIDIA's own terms for data use are not read here (data class unknown). The Zen pool limit never
;    stops a NVIDIA lane, and a NVIDIA 429 stops only the model it came from. The key is the one
;    OpenCode already stores for the provider; no key value is read or written by any lane.
;    Receipts, 2026-10-31, one content-free probe per model ("Reply with the single word ok.", an
;    empty throw-away directory, 110 s limit, through OpenCode's stored credential, no repo content).
;    Answered with text: openai/gpt-oss-20b (about 8 s), google/diffusiongemma-26b-a4b-it (6 s),
;    meta/muse-glimmer-30b (14 s), minimaxai/minimax-m3.1-flash (22 s),
;    nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning (3 s), nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b (5 s),
;    nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b (5 s), nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b (4 s),
;    poolside/laguna-xs-2.1 (4 s), stepfun-ai/step-5-preview (10 s). No text inside 110 s, which is
;    a timeout and not a refusal (recorded OTHER, not NO_ENTITLEMENT): deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4.1-flash,
;    google/gemma-4-31b-it, meta/llama-3.2-90b-vision-instruct, z-ai/glm-5.3-flash. Ten of fifteen
;    models answered, four timed out, one failed as below. provider.invalid-request after 1 s
;    (a function that is not deployed for the account, not a 401/402/403): meta/llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct.
;    The same keys listed the catalogue on 2026-10-26 and got 403 on chat, so a result here is a
;    dated measurement of one call, not a standing entitlement: re-probe before leaning on it.
; ASCII only (L3). phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27osOpencodeFree;

use t27os::editors::same_bytes;
use t27os::keys::RATE_COOLDOWN_S;

; --- prices --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// A price the catalog did not state: not zero, so not free.
pub const PRICE_UNKNOWN : u32 = 4294967295;

/// Free means both prices are zero. The name of a model plays no part.
pub fn is_free(input_nano : u32, output_nano : u32) -> bool {
    if (input_nano != 0) { return false; }
    if (output_nano != 0) { return false; }
    return true;
}

; --- providers -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const PROVIDER_ZEN : str = "opencode";
/// NVIDIA's hosted catalog (integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1, chat-completions) as OpenCode names it:
/// the provider "nvidia", the model "org/name" (the owner's free NVIDIA tokens, 2026-10-31).
pub const PROVIDER_NVIDIA : str = "nvidia";

/// The lane's embedded config (enabled_providers) names these two providers and no other (owner
/// condition 1; the global OpenCode config is not edited). Paid providers in the environment are not
/// selectable.
pub fn provider_allowed(provider : []const u8) -> bool {
    if (same_bytes(provider, PROVIDER_ZEN)) { return true; }
    if (same_bytes(provider, PROVIDER_NVIDIA)) { return true; }
    return false;
}

; --- content and data classes --------------------------------------------------------------------
/// A probe: no repository content at all.
pub const CC_NONE : u32 = 0;
/// Text that is already public.
pub const CC_PUBLIC : u32 = 1;
/// Anything not yet public: unmerged work, private repositories, internal notes.
pub const CC_NON_PUBLIC : u32 = 2;
/// A key, a token, a password, a personal datum, a payment detail.
pub const CC_SECRET : u32 = 3;

/// What the model's operator says it does with data (docs.opencode.ai/zen, 2026-10-31).
pub const DC_ZERO_RETENTION : u32 = 0;
pub const DC_NO_TRAINING : u32 = 1;
pub const DC_MAY_TRAIN : u32 = 2;
pub const DC_UNKNOWN : u32 = 3;

/// The two models the owner allowed to see non-public content (2026-10-31).
pub const NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A : str = "glm-5.3-flash-free";
pub const NONPUBLIC_MODEL_B : str = "deepseek-v4.1-flash-free";

/// The data class of a model as the docs stated it on 2026-10-31. A model the table does not know is
/// DC_UNKNOWN: new ids start restricted. This table is for the card's badge and the reviewer; the gate
/// below is the owner's named list, so a docs change cannot widen what leaves the machine.
pub fn data_class(model : []const u8) -> u32 {
    if (same_bytes(model, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A)) { return DC_ZERO_RETENTION; }
    if (same_bytes(model, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_B)) { return DC_ZERO_RETENTION; }
    if (same_bytes(model, "beam-free")) { return DC_NO_TRAINING; }
    if (same_bytes(model, "big-pickle")) { return DC_MAY_TRAIN; }
    if (same_bytes(model, "flint-40b-free")) { return DC_MAY_TRAIN; }
    if (same_bytes(model, "mimo-v2.6-flash-free")) { return DC_MAY_TRAIN; }
    return DC_UNKNOWN;
}

pub fn nonpublic_ok(model : []const u8) -> bool {
    if (same_bytes(model, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A)) { return true; }
    if (same_bytes(model, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_B)) { return true; }
    return false;
}

/// May this content go to this model? An unknown content class is a secret.
pub fn may_receive(model : []const u8, content : u32) -> bool {
    if (content == CC_NONE) { return true; }
    if (content == CC_PUBLIC) { return true; }
    if (content == CC_NON_PUBLIC) { return nonpublic_ok(model); }
    return false;
}

/// May this content go to this model of this provider? The owner's two named models are Zen models, so a
/// NVIDIA model, whatever its name, gets a probe or public text and nothing else: NVIDIA's own terms for
/// data use have not been read for this spec, so its data class is DC_UNKNOWN.
pub fn provider_may_receive(provider : []const u8, model : []const u8, content : u32) -> bool {
    if (same_bytes(provider, PROVIDER_NVIDIA)) {
        if (content == CC_NONE) { return true; }
        if (content == CC_PUBLIC) { return true; }
        return false;
    }
    return may_receive(model, content);
}

/// The one gate for a lane: the provider, the price and the content must all pass at once.
pub fn lane_ok(provider : []const u8, input_nano : u32, output_nano : u32, model : []const u8, content : u32) -> bool {
    if (provider_allowed(provider) == false) { return false; }
    if (is_free(input_nano, output_nano) == false) { return false; }
    return provider_may_receive(provider, model, content);
}

; --- task classes and routing --------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Where a job goes.
pub const ROUTE_FREE : u32 = 0;
pub const ROUTE_CLAUDE : u32 = 1;
pub const ROUTE_OWNER : u32 = 2;

/// Pool jobs: reading code, audits, docs, test drafts, small edits, UI drafts.
pub const TC_READ : u32 = 0;
pub const TC_AUDIT : u32 = 1;
pub const TC_DOCS : u32 = 2;
pub const TC_TEST_DRAFT : u32 = 3;
pub const TC_SMALL_EDIT : u32 = 4;
pub const TC_UI_DRAFT : u32 = 5;
/// Claude jobs: architecture, security, edits across files, release, very long context.
pub const TC_ARCH : u32 = 6;
pub const TC_SECURITY : u32 = 7;
pub const TC_MULTI_FILE : u32 = 8;
pub const TC_RELEASE : u32 = 9;
pub const TC_LONG_CONTEXT : u32 = 10;
/// Owner jobs: no lane starts them.
pub const TC_SECRET : u32 = 11;
pub const TC_CREDENTIAL : u32 = 12;
pub const TC_DELETE : u32 = 13;
pub const TC_UPSTREAM : u32 = 14;
pub const TC_PUBLISH : u32 = 15;
pub const TC_PAYMENT : u32 = 16;

/// The executor for a job. Only TC_SECURITY can be lifted to the pool, and only by the owner's
/// approval; an unknown class goes to Claude, the accountable executor, never to the pool.
pub fn route_task(task : u32, owner_approved_pool : bool) -> u32 {
    if (task <= TC_UI_DRAFT) { return ROUTE_FREE; }
    if (task >= TC_SECRET) {
        if (task <= TC_PAYMENT) { return ROUTE_OWNER; }
        return ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    }
    if (task == TC_SECURITY) {
        if (owner_approved_pool) { return ROUTE_FREE; }
    }
    return ROUTE_CLAUDE;
}

; --- lane state and the quota wait ---------------------------------------------------------------
pub const LS_AVAILABLE : u32 = 0;
pub const LS_WAITING_QUOTA : u32 = 1;
pub const LS_UNAVAILABLE : u32 = 2;
/// Listed free, never yet answered: a lane starts here, may be probed once, and gets no work until a
/// good answer. A listed price of 0 is not an entitlement (the NVIDIA keys listed 85 models on
/// 2026-10-26 and were refused on every chat call).
pub const LS_UNPROVEN : u32 = 3;
/// The provider refused this model for this account (HTTP 401, 402 or 403) although the catalog lists
/// it free. A fresh listing does not lift it; only the owner's re-arm does.
pub const LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT : u32 = 4;

/// 200 with a body.
pub const EV_OK : u32 = 0;
/// 429 with the error type FreeUsageLimitError: the whole pool, for the time the server gave.
pub const EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT : u32 = 1;
/// Any other 429: this model, at least RATE_COOLDOWN_S.
pub const EV_RATE_LIMIT : u32 = 2;
/// The model left the catalog or is no longer free.
pub const EV_GONE : u32 = 3;
/// A fresh catalog lists the model free again.
pub const EV_LISTED_FREE : u32 = 4;
/// Anything else (a 5xx, a timeout): the state does not change on a guess.
pub const EV_OTHER : u32 = 5;
/// HTTP 401, 402 or 403: the plan or the credit does not cover this model. Not a time limit.
pub const EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST : u32 = 6;
/// The owner allows one more probe for a refused model.
pub const EV_OWNER_REARM : u32 = 7;

/// Used when the server named no time. 3600 s, one hour, then a single new look.
pub const POOL_DEFAULT_WAIT_S : u64 = 3600;
/// No wait is taken longer than a week, whatever a header says.
pub const POOL_MAX_WAIT_S : u64 = 604800;
/// A model may be probed this many times, ever: the owner's word of 2026-10-31.
pub const PROBES_PER_MODEL : u32 = 1;

/// Does this event stop every model in the pool, not just the one that was called?
pub fn pool_wide(ev : u32) -> bool {
    return ev == EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT;
}

/// Turn what a call returned into one event. A 2xx counts only with text in the body (a thinking model
/// can answer 200 with an empty text); 401, 402 and 403 are a fact about the route first and the key
/// second (access-map), so they refuse the model, not the key.
pub fn event_from_status(status : u32, free_limit_type : bool, has_text : bool) -> u32 {
    if (status >= 200) {
        if (status < 300) {
            if (has_text) { return EV_OK; }
            return EV_OTHER;
        }
    }
    if (status == 429) {
        if (free_limit_type) { return EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT; }
        return EV_RATE_LIMIT;
    }
    if (status == 401) { return EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST; }
    if (status == 402) { return EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST; }
    if (status == 403) { return EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST; }
    if (status == 404) { return EV_GONE; }
    if (status == 410) { return EV_GONE; }
    return EV_OTHER;
}

/// Does an event seen on one lane reach another lane? A pool-wide event reaches every lane of the same
/// provider and no lane of another; any other event reaches only the model it happened to. The Zen
/// free-usage limit therefore never stops a NVIDIA lane. NVIDIA's own 429 is taken as per model until a
/// probe run shows an account-wide limit.
pub fn event_reaches_lane(ev : u32, event_provider : []const u8, event_model : []const u8, lane_provider : []const u8, lane_model : []const u8) -> bool {
    if (same_bytes(event_provider, lane_provider) == false) { return false; }
    if (pool_wide(ev)) { return true; }
    return same_bytes(event_model, lane_model);
}

pub fn next_state(state : u32, ev : u32) -> u32 {
    if (state == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT) {
        if (ev == EV_OWNER_REARM) { return LS_UNPROVEN; }
        return LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    }
    if (state == LS_UNAVAILABLE) {
        if (ev == EV_LISTED_FREE) { return LS_AVAILABLE; }
        return LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    }
    if (ev == EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST) { return LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT; }
    if (ev == EV_GONE) { return LS_UNAVAILABLE; }
    if (ev == EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT) { return LS_WAITING_QUOTA; }
    if (ev == EV_RATE_LIMIT) { return LS_WAITING_QUOTA; }
    if (ev == EV_OK) { return LS_AVAILABLE; }
    return state;
}

fn cap_wait(seconds : u64) -> u64 {
    if (seconds > POOL_MAX_WAIT_S) { return POOL_MAX_WAIT_S; }
    return seconds;
}

/// Seconds to wait after an event, given the server's Retry-After (0 when it gave none).
pub fn wait_seconds(ev : u32, retry_after_s : u64) -> u64 {
    if (ev == EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT) {
        if (retry_after_s == 0) { return POOL_DEFAULT_WAIT_S; }
        return cap_wait(retry_after_s);
    }
    if (ev == EV_RATE_LIMIT) {
        const asked : u64 = cap_wait(retry_after_s);
        if (asked < RATE_COOLDOWN_S) { return RATE_COOLDOWN_S; }
        return asked;
    }
    return 0;
}

/// May a lane be called now? A waiting lane is called again only after its time; an unavailable,
/// unproven or refused one is not called for work at all (an unproven one is only probed).
pub fn may_call(state : u32, now_s : u64, until_s : u64) -> bool {
    if (state == LS_AVAILABLE) { return true; }
    if (state == LS_WAITING_QUOTA) { return now_s >= until_s; }
    return false;
}

/// May a probe be sent? Only the first for a model, only with no repository content, and only to a
/// model that has not answered yet: never while its pool waits, after it was refused, or once it is gone.
pub fn probe_ok(done : u32, content : u32, state : u32) -> bool {
    if (done >= PROBES_PER_MODEL) { return false; }
    if (content != CC_NONE) { return false; }
    return state == LS_UNPROVEN;
}

; --- what the card shows -------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const BADGE_FREE : u32 = 0;
pub const BADGE_PAID : u32 = 1;
pub const BADGE_QUOTA : u32 = 2;
/// Listed free, but the provider refused it for this account.
pub const BADGE_NO_ACCESS : u32 = 3;
/// Listed free, not yet answered.
pub const BADGE_UNPROVEN : u32 = 4;

/// A paid model is shown paid; a free one is shown free, or limited by quota while it waits, or
/// unproven, or refused. Free never reads as unlimited, and a listing never reads as access.
pub fn badge(free : bool, state : u32) -> u32 {
    if (free == false) { return BADGE_PAID; }
    if (state == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT) { return BADGE_NO_ACCESS; }
    if (state == LS_UNPROVEN) { return BADGE_UNPROVEN; }
    if (state == LS_WAITING_QUOTA) { return BADGE_QUOTA; }
    return BADGE_FREE;
}

; --- tests ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
test free_means_both_prices_are_zero {
    assert is_free(0, 0);
    assert is_free(1, 0) == false;
    assert is_free(0, 1) == false;
    assert is_free(1, 1) == false;
}

test a_missing_price_is_not_zero {
    assert is_free(PRICE_UNKNOWN, 0) == false;
    assert is_free(0, PRICE_UNKNOWN) == false;
    assert is_free(PRICE_UNKNOWN, PRICE_UNKNOWN) == false;
}

test the_name_does_not_make_a_model_free_or_paid {
    assert lane_ok("opencode", 0, 0, "big-pickle", CC_PUBLIC);
    assert lane_ok("opencode", 5, 0, "model-x-free", CC_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("opencode", 0, 5, "model-x-free", CC_NONE) == false;
}

test only_zen_and_nvidia_are_selectable_and_no_paid_provider_is {
    assert provider_allowed("opencode");
    assert provider_allowed("nvidia");
    assert provider_allowed("openai") == false;
    assert provider_allowed("anthropic") == false;
    assert provider_allowed("openrouter") == false;
    assert provider_allowed("nvidia-nim") == false;
    assert provider_allowed("") == false;
    assert lane_ok("openai", 0, 0, "glm-5.3-flash-free", CC_PUBLIC) == false;
}

test a_nvidia_lane_needs_a_zero_price_like_any_other {
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_NONE);
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_PUBLIC);
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 3, 0, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 3, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_NONE) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", PRICE_UNKNOWN, PRICE_UNKNOWN, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_PUBLIC) == false;
}

test a_nvidia_model_gets_no_non_public_content_whatever_its_name {
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, "deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4.1-flash", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A, CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_B, CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert lane_ok("nvidia", 0, 0, "openai/gpt-oss-20b", CC_SECRET) == false;
    assert lane_ok("opencode", 0, 0, NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A, CC_NON_PUBLIC);
    assert data_class("openai/gpt-oss-20b") == DC_UNKNOWN;
}

test non_public_content_goes_only_to_the_two_named_models {
    assert may_receive("glm-5.3-flash-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC);
    assert may_receive("deepseek-v4.1-flash-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC);
    assert may_receive("big-pickle", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("flint-40b-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("mimo-v2.6-flash-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("beam-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("nemotron-3.5-lightning-free", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
    assert may_receive("a-model-nobody-has-seen", CC_NON_PUBLIC) == false;
}

test public_content_and_probes_may_go_to_any_free_model {
    assert may_receive("big-pickle", CC_PUBLIC);
    assert may_receive("beam-free", CC_PUBLIC);
    assert may_receive("nemotron-3.5-lightning-free", CC_PUBLIC);
    assert may_receive("a-model-nobody-has-seen", CC_NONE);
    assert may_receive("big-pickle", CC_NONE);
}

test a_secret_goes_to_no_model_and_an_unknown_class_is_a_secret {
    assert may_receive("glm-5.3-flash-free", CC_SECRET) == false;
    assert may_receive("deepseek-v4.1-flash-free", CC_SECRET) == false;
    assert may_receive("big-pickle", CC_SECRET) == false;
    assert may_receive("glm-5.3-flash-free", 4) == false;
    assert may_receive("glm-5.3-flash-free", 99) == false;
}

test the_named_models_keep_no_data_in_the_docs_table {
    assert data_class(NONPUBLIC_MODEL_A) == DC_ZERO_RETENTION;
    assert data_class(NONPUBLIC_MODEL_B) == DC_ZERO_RETENTION;
    assert data_class("beam-free") == DC_NO_TRAINING;
    assert data_class("big-pickle") == DC_MAY_TRAIN;
    assert data_class("flint-40b-free") == DC_MAY_TRAIN;
    assert data_class("mimo-v2.6-flash-free") == DC_MAY_TRAIN;
    assert data_class("nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free") == DC_UNKNOWN;
    assert data_class("a-model-nobody-has-seen") == DC_UNKNOWN;
}

test no_model_that_may_train_or_is_unknown_gets_non_public_content {
    assert data_class("big-pickle") == DC_MAY_TRAIN;
    assert nonpublic_ok("big-pickle") == false;
    assert data_class("nemotron-3.5-lightning-free") == DC_UNKNOWN;
    assert nonpublic_ok("nemotron-3.5-lightning-free") == false;
}

test the_pool_takes_reading_audit_docs_tests_edits_and_ui_drafts {
    assert route_task(TC_READ, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_AUDIT, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_DOCS, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_TEST_DRAFT, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_SMALL_EDIT, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_UI_DRAFT, false) == ROUTE_FREE;
}

test architecture_security_multi_file_release_and_long_context_stay_on_claude {
    assert route_task(TC_ARCH, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(TC_SECURITY, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(TC_MULTI_FILE, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(TC_RELEASE, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(TC_LONG_CONTEXT, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
}

test security_work_reaches_the_pool_only_with_the_owners_approval {
    assert route_task(TC_SECURITY, true) == ROUTE_FREE;
    assert route_task(TC_ARCH, true) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(TC_RELEASE, true) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
}

test the_owners_jobs_never_start_in_a_lane_approval_or_not {
    assert route_task(TC_SECRET, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_CREDENTIAL, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_DELETE, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_UPSTREAM, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_PUBLISH, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_PAYMENT, false) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_SECRET, true) == ROUTE_OWNER;
    assert route_task(TC_PAYMENT, true) == ROUTE_OWNER;
}

test an_unknown_job_goes_to_claude_never_to_the_pool {
    assert route_task(17, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(99, false) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
    assert route_task(99, true) == ROUTE_CLAUDE;
}

test the_probe_of_2026_10_31_puts_the_whole_pool_to_wait {
    assert pool_wide(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT);
    assert pool_wide(EV_RATE_LIMIT) == false;
    assert pool_wide(EV_GONE) == false;
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT) == LS_WAITING_QUOTA;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, 62220) == 62220;
}

test the_wait_follows_the_server_and_has_a_default_and_a_cap {
    assert wait_seconds(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, 0) == POOL_DEFAULT_WAIT_S;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, 100) == 100;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, 999999999) == POOL_MAX_WAIT_S;
}

test an_ordinary_429_waits_at_least_the_key_masters_cooldown {
    assert wait_seconds(EV_RATE_LIMIT, 0) == RATE_COOLDOWN_S;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_RATE_LIMIT, 5) == RATE_COOLDOWN_S;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_RATE_LIMIT, 120) == 120;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_RATE_LIMIT, 999999999) == POOL_MAX_WAIT_S;
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_RATE_LIMIT) == LS_WAITING_QUOTA;
}

test events_that_are_not_limits_wait_for_nothing {
    assert wait_seconds(EV_OK, 62220) == 0;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_GONE, 62220) == 0;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_LISTED_FREE, 10) == 0;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_OTHER, 10) == 0;
}

test a_waiting_lane_is_called_only_after_its_time {
    assert may_call(LS_AVAILABLE, 100, 0);
    assert may_call(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, 100, 200) == false;
    assert may_call(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, 200, 200);
    assert may_call(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, 201, 200);
    assert may_call(LS_UNAVAILABLE, 999999, 0) == false;
}

test a_model_that_leaves_the_catalog_is_unavailable_until_a_catalog_lists_it_free {
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_GONE) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, EV_GONE) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNAVAILABLE, EV_OK) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNAVAILABLE, EV_RATE_LIMIT) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNAVAILABLE, EV_OTHER) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNAVAILABLE, EV_LISTED_FREE) == LS_AVAILABLE;
}

test a_good_answer_ends_a_wait_and_an_unclear_one_changes_nothing {
    assert next_state(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, EV_OK) == LS_AVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_OTHER) == LS_AVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, EV_OTHER) == LS_WAITING_QUOTA;
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_LISTED_FREE) == LS_AVAILABLE;
}

test one_probe_per_model_with_no_repository_content_and_never_while_waiting {
    assert PROBES_PER_MODEL == 1;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NONE, LS_UNPROVEN);
    assert probe_ok(1, CC_NONE, LS_UNPROVEN) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_PUBLIC, LS_UNPROVEN) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NON_PUBLIC, LS_UNPROVEN) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NONE, LS_AVAILABLE) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NONE, LS_WAITING_QUOTA) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NONE, LS_UNAVAILABLE) == false;
    assert probe_ok(0, CC_NONE, LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT) == false;
}

test a_status_becomes_one_event {
    assert event_from_status(200, false, true) == EV_OK;
    assert event_from_status(200, false, false) == EV_OTHER;
    assert event_from_status(429, true, false) == EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT;
    assert event_from_status(429, false, false) == EV_RATE_LIMIT;
    assert event_from_status(401, false, false) == EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST;
    assert event_from_status(402, false, false) == EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST;
    assert event_from_status(403, false, false) == EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST;
    assert event_from_status(404, false, false) == EV_GONE;
    assert event_from_status(410, false, false) == EV_GONE;
    assert event_from_status(500, false, false) == EV_OTHER;
    assert event_from_status(503, false, true) == EV_OTHER;
    assert event_from_status(0, false, false) == EV_OTHER;
}

test a_listing_is_not_an_entitlement_and_a_refused_model_stays_refused_until_the_owner_re_arms {
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_AVAILABLE, EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_WAITING_QUOTA, EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT, EV_LISTED_FREE) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT, EV_OK) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT, EV_RATE_LIMIT) == LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT;
    assert next_state(LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT, EV_OWNER_REARM) == LS_UNPROVEN;
    assert may_call(LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT, 999999, 0) == false;
    assert wait_seconds(EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST, 100) == 0;
}

test a_model_gets_work_only_after_one_good_answer {
    assert may_call(LS_UNPROVEN, 999999, 0) == false;
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_OK) == LS_AVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_OTHER) == LS_UNPROVEN;
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_LISTED_FREE) == LS_UNPROVEN;
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_GONE) == LS_UNAVAILABLE;
    assert next_state(LS_UNPROVEN, EV_RATE_LIMIT) == LS_WAITING_QUOTA;
}

test the_zen_pool_limit_does_not_stop_a_nvidia_lane {
    assert event_reaches_lane(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, "opencode", "big-pickle", "opencode", "beam-free");
    assert event_reaches_lane(EV_FREE_USAGE_LIMIT, "opencode", "big-pickle", "nvidia", "openai/gpt-oss-20b") == false;
    assert event_reaches_lane(EV_RATE_LIMIT, "nvidia", "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "nvidia", "openai/gpt-oss-20b");
    assert event_reaches_lane(EV_RATE_LIMIT, "nvidia", "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "nvidia", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash") == false;
    assert event_reaches_lane(EV_ENTITLEMENT_LOST, "nvidia", "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "nvidia", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash") == false;
}

test the_card_never_shows_a_free_model_as_unlimited_or_a_listing_as_access {
    assert badge(true, LS_AVAILABLE) == BADGE_FREE;
    assert badge(true, LS_WAITING_QUOTA) == BADGE_QUOTA;
    assert badge(true, LS_UNPROVEN) == BADGE_UNPROVEN;
    assert badge(true, LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT) == BADGE_NO_ACCESS;
    assert badge(false, LS_AVAILABLE) == BADGE_PAID;
    assert badge(false, LS_WAITING_QUOTA) == BADGE_PAID;
    assert badge(false, LS_NO_ENTITLEMENT) == BADGE_PAID;
}
